sed command:
It is used to manipulate the data in file.like search and replace, delete the line etc
Search and Replace the string
sed -i 's/searchstring/replacestring/g' filename  s is subsitute, g is to global replace -i is to save. s and g will be used only for search and replace time
Search and replace the word except line 8
sed -i '8!s/searchstring/replacestring/g' filename
search and replace tab with space
sed -i '/s/\t/ /g' filename
Find and delete the line
sed -i '/searchstring/d' filename  here d is to delete the line
delete firstline alone
sed -i '1d' filename
delete first 2 line in file
sed -i '1,2d' filename
Insert empty line post each line
sed -i G filename
Delete empty line
sed -i '/^$/d' filename  here ^ is starting of line and $ end of line ,  here in our case it start with empty and end with empty
keep first 10 lines in file
sed -i -n 1,10p filename p is pick, just pick first 10 line alone
keep line apart from 2 to 10 in file
sed -i 3,10d filename
In VI editor , how to search and replace
Inside vi editor in esc mode do below
:%s/searchstring/replacestring/

