Linux Directory Service - Account Authentication:
There are 2 types of account
1.Local account - the account which we directly creating to the server using useradd
2.Directory account - consider we have 1000 user and 1000 server, we cant go and add all 1000 user in 1000 servers manually right.for that we have directory account. will have one server and have directory service installed in that. and all server will connected to this server.the directory server will have all user details configured.when the user tried to login to one server it will initiate the authentication to directory server, if data present there, it make authentication and connection will established to the server.In windows we have active directory which is directory server or service. like that we have many directory service.directory service installed in vm its directory server
If we want to communicate to server we use ssh secure shell protocol and if we want to communicate to directory server then we use ldap protocol

List of directory service:
active directory - its Windows product
idm(identity manager)  -  its is redhat one
winbind - used in linux to communicate with windows. also called as samba server.here we have all linux server and we have active directory which has all user details, then using this samba server, we will connect to windows and get authenticated
openldap - is open source directory server for linux or unix os
ibm directory server - product by ibm for directory service
jump cloud another directory service
LDAP - its light weight directory access protocol, it is used to communicate between client server(linux or windows) to directory server and vice versa

