top command:
Its used to list the process and real time view of the system. Once we give top it will go into interactive mode to come out press q.top provide current time, up time of the system, no of user active in system, then load average, total task running, out of that how many active, sleeping , waiting and zombie.Zombie means, if the task has parent process, that parent process was killed then that process will be in zombie.It will provide cpu details, what is ideal cpu, system cpu,user cpu, waiting cpu.It will provide physical and virtual memory details.mem means physical, swap means virtual. in mem it will show total, used , free etc.It will list top running process list. in that it will show process id(pid), which user is running that process, PR which is priority scheduling, NR is nice value, if nr +ve then low priority and -ve its high priority.it will provide for each process what is the virt virtual mem used, rem what is the ram mem used, shr what is the shared mem used, and it will provide what is the out of total what percentage of cpu and mem of the process and it show what command that process is running
To see particular user running process
top -u usernmae
To get the abosilute path of command running in  each process, when in interactive mode click c
To sort the process based on high mem usage press MP
To kill some process in interactive mode click k and give process id

